🚀 DevOps Interview Experience – Winjit Technologies (L1 Round | Hyderabad | 4+years )

Sharing a recent DevOps interview experience of one of the aspirants for the benefit of the community. 
Hope this helps aspiring engineers preparing for Cloud / DevOps / SRE roles.

📍 Company: Winjit Technologies
📍 Location: Hyderabad
📍 Round: L1 Technical

Below are some of the questions asked:

1️⃣ Tell me about your daily activities in your project.
(They wanted to understand real-time responsibilities like CI/CD management, infrastructure provisioning, monitoring, troubleshooting, etc.)

2️⃣ Explain the Maven lifecycle.
Phases like:
	•	validate
	•	compile
	•	test
	•	package
	•	verify
	•	install
	•	deploy

3️⃣ An EC2 server is running services like Jenkins, Docker, HTTPS etc. Which Linux command can show the running services on the server?
Commands like:
	•	systemctl status
	•	systemctl list-units --type=service
	•	ps -ef | grep <service>
	•	netstat -tulnp or ss -tulnp

4️⃣ If an EC2 instance was created using Terraform with a 50GB EBS volume, but someone manually increased it to 100GB from the AWS console and the state file is not updated, how will Terraform know about the change?
👉 By running terraform refresh or terraform plan, Terraform compares the real infrastructure with the state file and updates the state accordingly.

5️⃣ Explain the Terraform lifecycle.
Typical workflow:
	•	terraform init
	•	terraform plan
	•	terraform apply
	•	terraform destroy

6️⃣ Explain how Prometheus and Grafana work together.
	•	Prometheus collects metrics from targets using exporters and stores them as time-series data.
	•	Grafana connects to Prometheus as a data source and visualizes those metrics through dashboards and alerts.

7️⃣ Default ports of Prometheus and Grafana:
	•	Prometheus → 9090
	•	Grafana → 3000

💡 Tip: Most DevOps interviews focus on real-time scenarios rather than theoretical definitions, so try to connect every concept with practical use cases.
